  "status_text": "Take away any one of 31 key tests and a circuit can get by with one fewer bit-flipping gate. Lean checked a case with 127 tested sets on 13 switches, each requiring exactly one of two lights on. The full set needs three NOTs. Every subset that rules out a two-NOT budget must contain the same 31 tests, and deleting any one of those lets the rest fit that budget. The immediate inclusions between tested sets form a tree with at most four links at each node. The number of indispensable tests grows exponentially in this family (L-lib-1308).",
